Rosetta ab initio protocol. Ab initio folding of the TPR1 domain (PDB 1ELW, chain A) was performed with Rosetta 2020.03.61102 (linuxgccrelease, MPI build) using the AbinitioRelax application. 
The inputs were the native structure 1elw.pdb, the target sequence 1elw.fasta, Robetta-generated 3-mer and 9-mer fragment libraries (aat000_03_05.200_v1_3 and aat000_09_05.200_v1_3, Robetta job ID 61920), and the PSIPRED secondary-structure prediction t000_.psipred_ss2. 
The production run used mpiexec -n 24 AbinitioRelax.mpi.linuxgccrelease @flags, where the flags file specified -in:file:native 1elw.pdb, -in:file:fasta 1elw.fasta, -in:file:frag3 aat000_03_05.200_v1_3, -in:file:frag9 aat000_09_05.200_v1_3, 
-in:file:psipred_ss2 t000_.psipred_ss2, -nstruct 2500, -abinitio:relax, -use_filters true, -abinitio::increase_cycles 10, -abinitio::rg_reweight 0.5, -abinitio::rsd_wt_helix 0.5, -abinitio::rsd_wt_loop 0.5, -relax::fast, and -out:file:silent fold_silent.out. 
The default Rosetta scoring function for release 2020.03 was used without modification: score3/score4 in the centroid ab initio stages and ref2015 in the all-atom relax stage. 
The 2,500 decoys were generated across 24 MPI ranks, the top 1.0% (n = 25) were extracted with extract_pdbs.static.linuxgccrelease -in:file:silent fold_silent.out -out:pdb -in:file:tags Rosetta/top25_tags.txt, and all decoys were clustered with the 
Rosetta cluster application at a 3.0 Å RMSD radius. 

flags
-in:file:native ./1elw.pdb
-in:file:fasta ./1elw.fasta
-in:file:frag3 ./aat000_03_05.200_v1_3
-in:file:frag9 ./aat000_09_05.200_v1_3
-in:file:psipred_ss2 ./t000_.psipred_ss2
-nstruct 2500
-abinitio:relax
-use_filters true
-abinitio::increase_cycles 10
-abinitio::rg_reweight 0.5
-abinitio::rsd_wt_helix 0.5
-abinitio::rsd_wt_loop 0.5
-relax::fast
-out:file:silent ./fold_silent.out
